Source vs binaries
==================

CLI (`imprint-cli`) does not depend on GPUI. Distributing that binary is
covered by Apache-2.0 plus the licenses of its crates.io dependencies
(MIT, Apache-2.0, BSD, ISC, Unicode-3.0, MPL-2.0 at file level, and
similar permissive terms).

The desktop app (`imprint`, crate `imprint-app`) statically links GPUI
from the official Zed git tree. The `gpui` crate is Apache-2.0, but the
default dependency graph currently includes these crates from the same
tree, licensed GPL-3.0-or-later:

  ztracing
  zlog
  ztracing_macro

  https://github.com/zed-industries/zed

Until those crates are removed from GPUI's default graph (see
https://github.com/zed-industries/zed/issues/55470), distributing the
desktop binary is a combined work that must also comply with GPL-3.0.

